{"lok": [{"id": "lok", "headword": "लोक्", "headword_slp1": "lok", "fold": "lok", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "लोक् (I) vt. 1Ā (pres. लोकते) To see, to perceive.With अव-, to see, to perceive, e.g. नोलूकोऽप्यवलोकते यदि दिवा सूर्यस्य किं दूषणम्.With आ-, to see, to look at, to view, Bt.ii.24.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "लोक् Caus. (लोकयति-ते) 1. to look at, to view; 2. to know, to be aware of; 3. to shine; 4. to speak.With अव-, 1. to see, to look at, Bg.vi.13, R.viii.37; 2. to know, to learn, to ascertain, निर्गतस्तावदवलोकयामि कियदवशिष्टं रजन्या इति Sak.iv.; 3. to look after, to take care of.With आ-, 1. to see, to look at, to view, R.xiv.29; 2. to know, to ascertain; 3. to regard as, to take to be, तृणमिव जगज्जालमालोकयामः Bhartr.iii.66.With वि-, 1. to see, to perceive, to look at, इतश्चकोराक्षि विलोकयेति पूर्वानुशिष्टां निजगाद भोज्याम् R.vi.59, K.S.v.25, R.ii.11; 2. to look for, to search.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "लोक् (II) vi. 10Ā (pres. लोकयते) To shine.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "loka": [{"id": "loka", "headword": "लोक", "headword_slp1": "loka", "fold": "loka", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "लोक m. 1. Any division of the universe; (generally three Lokas are mentioned, viz., स्वर्ग, पृथ्वी and पाताल; but in fuller descriptions fourteen Lokas are enumerated, seven higher regions rising from the earth, viz., (1) भूर्लोक; (2) भुवर्लोक; (3) स्वर्लोक; (4) महर्लोक; (5) जनर्लोक; (6) तपर्लोक and (7) सत्यलोक, and seven lower regions descending from the earth one below the other, viz., (1) अतल; (2) वितल; (3) सुतल; (4) रसातल; (5) तलातल; (6) महातल and (7) पाताल), M.iv.219; 2. the earth; (इह लोके ‘in this world’); 3. the human race, mankind, आकृष्टलीलान्नरलोकपालान् R.vi.1, M.viii.42; 4. the subjects (as op. to the king), स हि सर्वस्य लोकस्य युक्तदंडतया मन आददे R.iv.8; 5. a class, a community, शशाम तेन क्षितिपाललोकः R.vii.3, v.64; 6. a region, a province, a district; 7. looking, sight; 8. the number ‘seven’; 9. common life, (op. to Śāstra); 10. common usage, (op. to वेद ‘Vedic idiom’), प्रियतद्धिता दाक्षिणाया यथा लोकवेदयोरिति प्रयोक्तव्य लौकिकवैदिकेष्विति प्रयुंजते Patanjali, अतोऽस्मि लोके वेदे च प्रथितः पुरुषोत्तमः Bg.xv.18", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["लोकः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["lokaH"]}], "lokatiga": [{"id": "lokAtiga", "headword": "लोकातिग", "headword_slp1": "lokAtiga", "fold": "lokatiga", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "लोक-अतिग a. extraordinary, supernatural.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "lokatisaya": [{"id": "lokAtiSaya", "headword": "लोकातिशय", "headword_slp1": "lokAtiSaya", "fold": "lokatisaya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "लोक-अतिशय a. superior to the world.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "lokaDipa": [{"id": "lokADipa", "headword": "लोकाधिप", "headword_slp1": "lokADipa", "fold": "lokaDipa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "लोक-अधिप m. 1. a king; 2. a god, a deity.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["लोकाधिपः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["lokADipaH"]}], "lokaDipati": [{"id": "lokADipati", "headword": "लोकाधिपति", "headword_slp1": "lokADipati", "fold": "lokaDipati", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "लोक-अधिपति m. the lord of the world.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["लोकाधिपतिः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["lokADipatiH"]}], "lokanuraga": [{"id": "lokAnurAga", "headword": "लोकानुराग", "headword_slp1": "lokAnurAga", "fold": "lokanuraga", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "लोक-अनुराग m. universal benevolence, philanthrophy.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["लोकानुरागः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["lokAnurAgaH"]}], "lokantara": [{"id": "lokAMtara", "headword": "लोकांतर", "headword_slp1": "lokAMtara", "fold": "lokantara", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "लोक-अंतर n. another world, लोकांतरं गम् ‘to die,’ R.i.69